==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Indo-European|gʷeih₃w-|to live|lang=la}}. Cognate with Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrl|жити|tr=žiti|lang=cu}}, Ancient Greek {{term|sc=polytonic|βίος|tr=bios|lang=grc}}, Sanskrit {{term|sc=Deva|जीवति|tr=jīvati|lang=sa}}.

===Verb===
{{la-verb|vivo|vīvō|vivere|vīvere|vixi|vīxī|victum|vīctum}}

# I [[live]]
#* {{term|w:en:Catiline Orations|Catiline Orations}} by [[w:en:Cicero|Cicero]] (Latin text and English translations may be found [http://www.perseus.tufts.edu/hopper/text.jsp?doc=Perseus:text:1999.02.0010:text=Catil.:speech=1:section=2 here])
#*: ''O tempora, o mores! Senatus haec intellegit, consul videt; hic tamen '''vivit'''. '''Vivit'''?''
#*:: Shame on the age and on its principles! The senate is aware of these things; the consul sees them; and yet this man '''lives'''. '''Lives'''!
# I'm [[alive]], I [[survive]]
# I [[reside]]

====Derived terms====
*[[ita vivam#Latin|ita vivam]] (as true as I live)
*[[ne vivam si]] (may I die if)
*[[si vivo]] (if I live)

====Inflection====
{{la-conj-3rd|vīv|vīx|vīct|11=viv|22=vix|33=vict}}

====Synonyms====
*[[spiro#Latin|spiro]]

